## Storybook rules

- Stories colocate with components and export `Meta`/`StoryObj`.
- Group titles like Chakra's component overview: Layout, Typography, Buttons, Forms, Overlays, Disclosure, Feedback, Data Display (e.g. `Forms/Textarea`, `Layout/Flex`).
- Add controls for all recipe variant props using `variantMap`.
- Panda `ConditionalValue` props (gap, wrap, grow, direction, style props) infer as Storybook **object** controls. Override with select / boolean / number, and set `parameters.controls.include` to the knobs for that component. Do not leave "Set object" editors for layout props.
- Provide at least these stories: Default, Disabled, Sizes, States (hover/focus via pseudo‑class style if demonstrable), and With label/description if applicable.

Story template:

```tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react';
import { Component } from './Component';
import { someRecipe } from '@becket-ui/tokens/recipes';

const meta: Meta<typeof Component> = {
  title: 'Forms/Component',
  component: Component,
  argTypes: {
    // Map controls from variantMap
    // size: { control: { type: 'select' }, options: someRecipe.variantMap.size },
  },
};
export default meta;

type Story = StoryObj<typeof Component>;

export const Default: Story = { args: {} };
```

