## Coding style carry‑over (highlights)

- Prefer inline logic over unnecessary abstractions, especially in JSX; keep mental overhead low.
- Use inversion of control for branching complexity; components accept render props/children when extensibility is needed.
- Reduce nesting with guard clauses.

---

## When adding a new component, do this

1) Add/extend a Panda recipe in `@becket-ui/tokens` if needed, export it, and regenerate Panda artifacts.
2) Implement the React component in `@becket-ui/react` using the API rules and recipe. Meet WCAG 2.2 AA before review.
3) Add a Storybook file with controls for all variants and key states. `@storybook/addon-a11y` must be clean on Default (local; not CI).
4) Add Vitest coverage: axe-core via the private `@becket-ui/a11y` helper ([MAV-45](https://kolmena.atlassian.net/browse/MAV-45) / [MAV-46](https://kolmena.atlassian.net/browse/MAV-46)) plus keyboard tests if the primitive has APG behavior. Do **not** add Playwright or Chromatic for this.
5) Keep names and imports consistent; avoid mutations; use tokens over literals.

---

## Accessibility tests (mandatory)

Interactive primitives **do not ship** without automated a11y tests. Manual Storybook checks are extra, not a substitute.

| Layer | Tool | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **CI gate** | axe-core in **Vitest + jsdom** + Testing Library | `@becket-ui/react` tests, helper `@becket-ui/a11y` (`private: true`) |
| **Keyboard / APG** | `@testing-library/user-event` | Dialog, Drawer, Menu, Tabs, Tooltip, Switch (Tab, Escape, arrows) |
| **Static** | Biome a11y rules or `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` when [MAV-9](https://kolmena.atlassian.net/browse/MAV-9) lands | lint |
| **Local authoring** | `@storybook/addon-a11y` | Storybook panel only |

**Out:** Playwright, Storybook test-runner, Chromatic, Cypress, Pa11y, Lighthouse-CI, a from-scratch WCAG engine, publishing `@becket-ui/a11y` on npm in 0.1.0.

**jsdom cannot prove** color-contrast, 24×24 target size (2.5.8), or painted focus rings. Disable those axe rules in CI. They stay Storybook addon + a recorded keyboard/contrast pass (C3).

Do not take stale `vitest-axe@0.1.0` as the long-term matcher — call `axe.run` from a thin helper we own.

This MDC governs all component contributions. Always align with PandaCSS docs (`panda` recipes, patterns, tokens) and update recipes first when introducing new visual variants.

